  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The new-arrivals workbench",
    "overview": "This is a record of the current inventory implementation, extracted from apps/web/app/globals.css, its React components and the bounded theme styles in apps/api/relicrat/theme_values.py. The new-arrivals workbench uses warm ivory, white surfaces, charcoal ink and restrained burgundy actions to make physical copies easy to record and find. Plain labeled controls and text-led records keep collection information prominent, without paper texture or faux-vintage controls.\n\nThe owner approved these factory theme values on 2026-10-31, including sans body/headings, balanced spacing, soft corners and comfortable density. The forest and light-gold After hours preset is the dark companion. Approval covers application theme values; brand-wide master specifications, proposed logos, mascot extensions and navigation layouts remain separate decisions. Owners can explicitly preview and apply their own supported theme. This record describes the implementation for review, not deployment or production readiness.\n\nThe separate frozen progress report through PR #14 retains its own [historical design record](docs/design/project-dashboard.md) and [preserved sidecar](.impeccable/project-dashboard-design.json); it is not current application guidance. The original add-first and direct-build choices do not establish a standing build-path preference.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "System UI sans for an Operate workflow.",
      "Approved ivory, charcoal and burgundy factory palette with a forest/gold dark companion.",
      "Flat paper and ruled rows with one explicit selection.",
      "Visible save, loading, conflict and recovery states.",
      "Responsive reading order and keyboard focus."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Explicit State Rule",
        "body": "Pair state colors with readable text and programmatic status; color alone does not establish a saved record.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Separate Save Rule",
        "body": "Make confirmed copy, photo and location saves distinguishable; choosing a location immediately saves a revision-checked move and confirms its destination beside the selector. Creating a location remains a separate save.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve visible labels, focus outlines and textual status alongside color.",
      "**Do** use contained photos of the physical copy as user data.",
      "**Do** keep copy/photo/catalog/location creation separate, save location choices immediately, and require explicit review after uncertain writes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** turn the historical progress report into app design guidance.",
      "**Don't** imply saved data, identity or production readiness through visual state alone.",
      "**Don't** treat factory-theme approval as approval for proposed logos, mascot extensions, layouts or brand-wide master specifications.",
      "**Don't** apply paper texture or faux-vintage controls across the product interface."
    ]
  }
